Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Sometimes it is not safe to use certain medicines at the same time. Some drugs can affect your thyroid hormone levels and also make levothyroxine less effective.
If you use any of the following drugs, avoid taking them within 4 hours before or 4 hours after you use levothyroxine:
- calcium carbonate (Alka-Mints, Caltrate, Os-Cal, Oyster Shell Calcium, Rolaids Soft Chew, Tums, and others);
- sevelamer, lanthanum;
- cholestyramine, colesevelam, colestipol;
- iron supplements, including ferrous sulfate;
- sucralfate;
- sodium polystyrene sulfonate (Kalexate, Kayexalate, Kionex);
- stomach acid reducers - esomeprazole, lansoprazole, omeprazole, rabeprazole, Nexium, Prilosec, Prevacid, Protonix, Zegerid, and others (this applies to most brands of levothyroxine except for Tirosint-SOL); or
- antacids that contain aluminum or magnesium - Gaviscon, Maalox, Milk of Magnesia, Mintox, Mylanta, Pepcid Complete, and others.
Tell your doctor about all your other medicines, especially:
- orlistat;
- phenobarbital, rifampin;
- ketamine, steroid medicines such as dexamethasone;
Triplet: ["Levothyroxine", "has interaction warning", "avoid within 4 hours before or after use"]

The relation 'has interaction warning' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug requires patients to avoid taking the object substance within a specified time frame before or after use to prevent reduced effectiveness or adverse effects.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'should be avoided with': Patients taking the subject drug should avoid the substance or activity specified by the object entity.
B. 'reduces risk of': The subject drug is used to prevent or lower the risk of the medical event or condition specified by the object entity.
C. 'has duration of treatment': The subject drug is typically taken for the length of time specified by the object entity.
D. 'has warning': The subject drug carries a safety warning or precaution about the risk or situation specified by the object entity.
E. 'has administration instruction': The subject drug should be taken or used in the manner specified by the object entity (for example with food or at a fixed time).
F. None of the above.

Answer:
